From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ats0c <ats0c@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos9830: use exact big frequencies in ufc
 tables

The UFC driver publishes the first column of its tables as the virtual
CPU frequency table in /sys/power/cpufreq_table.  On Exynos 990 the rows
that select a new big cluster frequency carry a virtual value about
2.5 MHz below that frequency (2623359 for 2626000, 1999511 for 2002000,
and so on); only the top row, 2730000, is exact.

The IPM/SPA engine of current Game Optimizing Service builds its CPU
model by matching each cluster's frequencies, divided by a power of two,
against the virtual table, and requires at least 60% of them to match
exactly.  The big cluster matches 1 of 22, so SPA refuses to create its
system ("Failed to match big cluster virtual frequencies") and Game
Booster's performance monitor gets no FPS, CPU or GPU data.

Use the exact big cluster frequency for those 21 virtual values in all
four tables.  The cluster columns are unchanged and every table stays
strictly decreasing, so the kernel maps each row to the same cluster
limits as before.  A minimum limit written with one of the old values
still selects the same row; a maximum limit written with one selects
the next lower row.
